          "text": "Associated symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Coryza. No cough, shortness of breath, or gastrointestinal symptoms. Oral intake okay."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Rash"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pink, blanching, non-itchy truncal rash appeared 24 hours after fever decreased, then spread to neck and proximal limbs; now fading. Examination: faint resolving blanching macular/maculopapular rash on lower trunk/back, possibly a few lesions on proximal thighs; no rash on palms or soles, no vesicles, target lesions, or purpura."
      }
    },
